// The sword family (src/character/weaponDef.ts, CHARACTERS.md, *Weapons and shields*): parts laid
// along the weapon's axis in metres, 0 at the middle of the grip and the blade's way positive.
// profile: [t along the part, width across the blade's flat, thickness through it]; 0, 0 is a point.
// Details are oversized, as the rest of the world is, so the tier reads from the camera. Each tier
// is gear of its own for items to name: "sword.crude", "sword.standard", "sword.ornate"; the item's
// tint colours the `metal` parts (bronze, iron, steel).
{
  name: "Sword",
  grip: "mainHand",
  tiers: {
    // A plain blade, a bar guard of the same metal, a wrapped grip and no pommel - a smith's first.
    crude: {
